# Rust
target/
Cargo.lock
# ...except the contracts workspace's. soroban-env-host depends on
# ed25519-dalek ">=2.0.0", so an unpinned CI resolve picks up 3.0.0, which it
# does not compile against — the deployable WASM has to build from a
# reproducible dependency set, not whatever crates.io published today.
!contracts/Cargo.lock
# The Rust SDK's lockfile is committed for the same reason: it is a published
# library, but CI should test one pinned dependency set rather than whatever
# crates.io resolved to this morning. A dependent's own resolution is
# unaffected — cargo ignores a library's lockfile when it is used as a
# dependency.
!sdk/rust/Cargo.lock
test_snapshots/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
.env
.env.local

